solution.text:
The molecular formula of ethane is $\mathrm{C}_{2} \mathrm{H}_{\mathrm{6}}$ To get its fourth homologue, we have to add
$$
\begin{array}{r}
4 \times \mathrm{CH}_{2}=\mathrm{C}_{4} \mathrm{H}_{8} \text { to it. } \\
\mathrm{C}_{2} \mathrm{H}_{6}+\mathrm{C}_4 \mathrm{H}_{8}=\mathrm{C}_6 \mathrm{H}_{14}
\end{array}
$$
$\mathrm{C}_{6} \mathrm{H}_{14}$ is the molecular formula of hexane. Thus, hexane is the fourth homologue of ethane.
